{
  "name": "How to Document Hail Damage for Your Evaluation in Alvarado",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Note the Storm Details — As soon as possible, write down the date, approximate time, and duration of the hailstorm. Also, make a note of the general size of the hail if you observed it (e.g., pea-sized, golf ball-sized). This timeline helps confirm when the damage occurred.",
      "text": "Step 1: Note the Storm Details — As soon as possible, write down the date, approximate time, and duration of the hailstorm. Also, make a note of the general size of the hail if you observed it (e.g., pea-sized, golf ball-sized). This timeline helps confirm when the damage occurred.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Take Ground-Level Photos — Before a professional arrives, take wide-angle photos of your home from different angles, capturing the roofline and any visible damage to siding, gutters, windows, or vehicles. Then, take close-up photos of any clearly visible damage from the ground, such as dents in gutters or obvious missing shingles.",
      "text": "Step 2: Take Ground-Level Photos — Before a professional arrives, take wide-angle photos of your home from different angles, capturing the roofline and any visible damage to siding, gutters, windows, or vehicles. Then, take close-up photos of any clearly visible damage from the ground, such as dents in gutters or obvious missing shingles.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Gather Insurance Documents — Locate your current homeowner's insurance policy and policy number. Having this information readily available will streamline communication with both your insurance provider and your chosen roofing contractor.",
      "text": "Step 3: Gather Insurance Documents — Locate your current homeowner's insurance policy and policy number. Having this information readily available will streamline communication with both your insurance provider and your chosen roofing contractor.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Preserve Related Records — If you have any previous roof inspection reports, maintenance records, or even photos from before the storm, keep them handy. These can help establish the pre-storm condition of your roof.",
      "text": "Step 4: Preserve Related Records — If you have any previous roof inspection reports, maintenance records, or even photos from before the storm, keep them handy. These can help establish the pre-storm condition of your roof.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Avoid Climbing the Roof — For your safety and to prevent further damage, do not climb onto the roof yourself. Leave that to the trained professionals from Discounted Roofing Co., who have the proper safety equipment and expertise to inspect it safely and thoroughly.",
      "text": "For a complete hail damage evaluation in Alvarado, schedule your inspection with Discounted Roofing Co. after documenting what you can.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
